window.AWD_SCRIPTS = {"A": "<p><i>v3, 2026-10-09: <b>sell the meeting, not the website.</b> Rewritten from Johnny's new flow. Caller: Johnny (Johnathon Ghormley). For businesses with <b>no website</b> (or only Facebook / Google / a free builder address). Old version: Old Scripts/Call Script - List A (No Website) v2.3.</i></p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> book a <b>15-minute Zoom (or a quick stop-by)</b> to show them a free homepage design. Don't sell the website on this call. The design and the meeting sell it.</p>\n<p><b>Before you dial (30 seconds in the CRM):</b> owner's name, business, city, Abby's <b>Opener</b> (something real and nice: their reviews, years in business, a job they posted). Check whether Dex has <b>already built</b> their homepage (design note / CRM history), because that decides which line you use in step 4.</p>\n<p><b>Keep it honest:</b> only say things that are true. Use the referral opener only for real referrals; no made-up referrals, no claiming a site is built when it isn't.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>1. Confirm who you've got</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, is this <b>[business]</b>?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>They say yes.</i></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Is this <b>[owner]</b>?\" (If it's someone else, go to step 9.)</blockquote>\n<h3>2. Opener: compliment + the website question</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, good. My name's Johnny, I'm a local web designer here in Bay Area Houston. I came across y'all on Google, and it looks like y'all do really, really good work. <b>[Abby's opener, e.g. \"45 five-star reviews, that's no joke.\"]</b><br>But I didn't see a website for y'all. Is there a reason for that?\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>If someone actually referred this lead to you</b> (use only when it's true; put their real name in):</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, good. I was referred by <b>[referrer]</b>, and they said y'all's company does really, really good work. I found y'all on Google, but I don't see a website. Is there a reason for that?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Then stop and let them answer. Whatever they say, agree first, then turn it.</i></p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I don't really need one. I get enough business.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Honestly, that's how it is with most of the good businesses I find. Word of mouth is the best kind. But when somebody hears about y'all, the first thing they do is Google you, and right now they don't find much.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"We've already got a Google page / Facebook.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That's good, keep it. A website just sits right next to it, so when someone Googles y'all, you look like the real deal, not just a listing.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"Never got around to it / too expensive.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That's what I hear the most. Most places want a thousand to three thousand bucks. That's exactly why I do it the way I do.\"</p>\n<h3>3. What a website does for them</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Basically, man, with a website, when someone Googles y'all, it's one of the first things that pops up, and they see all y'all's work. It shows a level of credibility a lot of people really appreciate. You can put your work and your services right on there.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>4. Who you are + the offer (the meeting)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"I'm just starting my own web design business, so you'd be working directly with me, the actual designer. No big agency, no call center. Later down the line I'd like to grow, but right now it's me.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>Pick the line that's true:</b></p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Dex has NOT built it yet:</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Here's what I'd like to do: I'll build y'all a homepage <b>for free</b>, and then we hop on a quick Zoom, or I stop by, and look at it together.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Dex HAS already built it:</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"I actually went ahead and put a homepage together for y'all already, <b>for free</b>. I'd love to show it to you. We can hop on a quick Zoom, or I can stop by, and look at it together.\"</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"If you like it, it's <b>200 bucks</b> and it's yours. If you don't, no big deal. Maybe refer me to a friend, and I'll go play with some trains.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>5. Photos and their work</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Do y'all have photos of some jobs you've done, or your work, that you'd be proud to show off?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>They say yes.</i></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, cool. Text me a few to <b>832-508-0059</b> and I'll put them right in, so it actually looks like y'all.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>6. Book the meeting (this is the win)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"So what works better for a quick 15 minutes, <b>[day] morning or [day] afternoon</b>? Zoom, or would you rather I just stop by?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"check\">\n<li>Day and time (offer two choices, don't ask \"when are you free?\")</li>\n<li>Zoom or in person (if in person: the address)</li>\n<li>Best number to text the link / reminder, and an email if they use one</li>\n<li>Main services they want people to find them for</li>\n<li>Areas they cover / where they're located</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Perfect. I'll text you to confirm. Talk to you <b>[day]</b>.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>In the CRM:</b> call status <b>Follow Up</b>, follow-up date = the meeting day, note \"Meeting [day/time], Zoom/in person\". If Dex hasn't built the design yet, ask Claude to have Dex build it <b>before</b> the meeting.</p>\n<h3>7. If they ask about price (keep it short)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"It's <b>200 bucks</b> one time and the website's yours. If you want, I'll set up the web address for you too, that's 25. And if you want me to host it and manage it for you month to month, it's a small fee of <b>50 a month</b>. If you don't, no big deal. 200 bucks, the website's yours.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>8. Objections</h3>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I'm not interested.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"No problem at all. Can I just send you the link to what I'd build, and you look whenever? No call needed.\" (If no again: \"Totally fine, thanks for your time.\")</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"Just send me something.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Even better. What's the best number to text it to? And if you like it, we'll do a quick 10-minute call after.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I don't have time for a meeting.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Totally get it. It's 15 minutes, and I'll work around you, early morning, lunch, after hours. Or I'll text you the link and you look whenever.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"What's the catch?\" / \"Is this a scam?\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Fair question. No catch. You don't pay anything unless you like it, and if you buy it, it's yours. Nothing to sign today.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"How much?\"</b> → step 7.</li>\n<li><b>\"$50 a month is a lot.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That part's optional. Pay the 200 and it's yours, and you can host it yourself. The 50 is only if you want me to handle everything.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"My nephew / a friend is going to build one.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That's great. I'll still put one together free, and you can compare. No pressure either way.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Asks not to be called again:</b> \"Understood, I'll take you off my list. Have a good one.\" Log <b>Asked not to call</b> (the CRM disqualifies them automatically).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. If someone else answers</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, this is Johnny, I'm a local web designer. I'm trying to reach <b>[owner]</b> about the business's website. Is he/she around?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Not in:</b> \"No problem. When's a good time to catch him/her? And is there a better number for them?\"</li>\n<li><b>\"What's it about?\":</b> \"I'd like to show them a free homepage design for the business. Takes 15 minutes.\"</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>10. Voicemail (under 20 seconds)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnny, a local web designer. I came across <b>[business]</b> on Google, y'all have great reviews, but I didn't see a website. I'd love to build y'all one for free and show it to you. Call or text me at <b>832-508-0059</b>. Again, 832-508-0059.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>11. Text after a voicemail or no answer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi [name], it's Johnny, local web designer. Just left you a voicemail. I'd love to build [business] a free website and show it to you on a quick 15-min Zoom. No cost unless you love it. 832-508-0059\"</blockquote>\n<h3>12. The meeting (15 minutes)</h3>\n<p>1. Quick thanks, ask how business is going (1 min).</p>\n<p>2. Show the homepage on their phone or the Zoom screen. Point out: their name and services up top, the tap-to-call button, their photos, their reviews (3-5 min).</p>\n<p>3. Ask: \"What do you think? Anything you'd change?\" Write it all down.</p>\n<p>4. <b>Likes it:</b> \"Awesome. It's 200 and it's yours. Want me to set up the web address too, and do you want me to host and manage it, or handle that yourself?\" Send the payment link from the CRM (pick the matching package). CRM: <b>Won</b>.</p>\n<p>5. <b>Wants changes:</b> \"Easy, I'll fix those and send it over by [day].\" Ask Dex to revise.</p>\n<p>6. <b>No:</b> \"No worries at all. Do you know anyone else who could use one?\" Log the reason.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>Rules:</b> dial by hand, be honest, never promise anything not in Offer &amp; Pricing. Respect \"don't call me\" right away. Log every call in the CRM.</p>", "B": "<p><i>v3, 2026-10-09: <b>sell the meeting, not the website.</b> Same flow as Call Script - List A (No Website), adjusted for businesses that <b>already have a website or own a domain</b>. Caller: Johnny (Johnathon Ghormley). Old version: Old Scripts/Call Script - List B (Has Website) v2.3.</i></p>\n<p><b>Goal:</b> book a <b>15-minute Zoom (or a quick stop-by)</b> to show them a free side-by-side redesign. Never trash their current site. Show them something better and let them compare.</p>\n<p><b>Before you dial (1 minute):</b> open their site <b>on your phone</b>. Note one or two specific, fair problems from Abby's <b>Website notes</b> (small text on a phone, no tap-to-call, looks dated, slow, missing services). Note the owner's name, business, city and Abby's <b>Opener</b>. Check whether Dex has <b>already built</b> their redesign.</p>\n<p><b>Keep it honest:</b> only say things that are true. Use the referral opener only for real referrals; no made-up referrals, no claiming a redesign is built when it isn't.</p>\n<hr>\n<h3>1. Confirm who you've got</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, is this <b>[business]</b>?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>They say yes.</i></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Is this <b>[owner]</b>?\" (If it's someone else, go to step 9.)</blockquote>\n<h3>2. Opener: compliment + their website</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, good. My name's Johnny, I'm a local web designer here in Bay Area Houston. I came across y'all on Google, and it looks like y'all do really, really good work. <b>[Abby's opener]</b><br>I pulled up y'all's website on my phone. Y'all have good info on there, but <b>[one specific, fair issue: the text is pretty small on a phone / there's no button to tap and call / it looks like it hasn't been updated in a while]</b>. Who put that site together for y'all?\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>If someone actually referred this lead to you</b> (use only when it's true; put their real name in):</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, good. I was referred by <b>[referrer]</b>, and they said y'all's company does really, really good work. I pulled up y'all's website on my phone, and <b>[one specific, fair issue]</b>. Who put that site together for y'all?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>Let them talk. Agree first, then turn it.</i></p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"My nephew / a friend built it.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That's awesome, that's how a lot of good sites start. I'm not saying throw it out. I'd just love to show y'all what it could look like today.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"It works fine for us.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Good to hear. Have you looked at it on your phone lately? That's where most people see it now.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"We pay a company for it.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Gotcha. I'll put a version together anyway, free, and you can compare. If yours is better, you've lost nothing.\"</p>\n<h3>3. What a modern website does for them</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Basically, when someone Googles y'all, the website's one of the first things they see. If it's clean and easy on a phone, they see all y'all's work and it shows a level of credibility people really appreciate. You can put your work and your services right up front.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>4. Who you are + the offer (the meeting)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"I'm just starting my own web design business, so you'd be working directly with me, the actual designer. No big agency, no call center.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>Pick the line that's true:</b></p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Dex has NOT built it yet:</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Here's what I'd like to do: I'll take what's on y'all's site and build a fresh version <b>for free</b>, same info, your same feel, just modern and easy on a phone. Then we hop on a quick Zoom, or I stop by, and look at them side by side.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Dex HAS already built it:</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"I actually went ahead and put a fresh version of y'all's homepage together already, <b>for free</b>. I'd love to show it to you side by side with the current one. Quick Zoom, or I can stop by.\"</p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"If you like mine, it's <b>200 bucks</b> and it's yours, and you keep your same web address. If you don't, no big deal. Maybe refer me to a friend, and I'll go play with some trains.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>5. Photos and their work</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Do y'all have photos of some jobs you've done, or your work, that you'd be proud to show off? Newer ones than what's on the site?\"</blockquote>\n<p><i>They say yes.</i></p>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Okay, cool. Text me a few to <b>832-508-0059</b> and I'll put them right in.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>6. Book the meeting (this is the win)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"So what works better for a quick 15 minutes, <b>[day] morning or [day] afternoon</b>? Zoom, or would you rather I just stop by?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"check\">\n<li>Day and time (offer two choices)</li>\n<li>Zoom or in person (if in person: the address)</li>\n<li>Best number to text the link / reminder, and an email if they use one</li>\n<li>Anything they wish their current site did better</li>\n<li>Who handles their web address now (just so you know; don't ask for passwords)</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Perfect. I'll text you to confirm. Talk to you <b>[day]</b>.\"</blockquote>\n<p><b>In the CRM:</b> call status <b>Follow Up</b>, follow-up date = the meeting day, note \"Meeting [day/time], Zoom/in person\". If Dex hasn't built the redesign yet, ask Claude to have Dex build it <b>before</b> the meeting.</p>\n<h3>7. If they ask about price (keep it short)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"It's <b>200 bucks</b> one time to switch, and the website's yours. You keep your same web address and email. If you want me to host it and manage it for you month to month, it's a small fee of <b>50 a month</b>. If you don't, no big deal. 200 bucks, it's yours.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>8. Objections</h3>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I already have a website.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Totally, and I'm not saying get rid of it. I'll build a free version side by side. If yours is better, you've lost nothing.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I just paid for my website.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Makes sense, keep it if it's working. If it's not bringing in calls, the new one's free to look at, and switching is 200 one time.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"What happens to my domain and email?\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"You keep your same web address, in your name, and your email stays exactly how it is. I just point the address at the new site.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I'm not interested.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"No problem. Can I just text you the link once it's done, and you look whenever?\" (If no again: \"Totally fine, thanks for your time.\")</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"I don't have time for a meeting.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"Totally get it. It's 15 minutes, and I'll work around you. Or I'll text you the link and you look whenever.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"What's the catch?\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"No catch. Nothing to pay unless you like it, and you keep your web address either way.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>\"How much?\"</b> → step 7.</li>\n<li><b>\"$50 a month is a lot. / I pay less now.\"</b></li>\n</ul>\n<p>  &gt; \"That part's optional. Pay the 200 and it's yours. The 50 is only if you want me to handle hosting and changes.\"</p>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Asks not to be called again:</b> \"Understood, I'll take you off my list. Have a good one.\" Log <b>Asked not to call</b> (the CRM disqualifies them automatically).</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>9. If someone else answers</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi, this is Johnny, I'm a local web designer. I'm trying to reach <b>[owner]</b> about the business's website. Is he/she around?\"</blockquote>\n<ul class=\"dot\">\n<li><b>Not in:</b> \"No problem. When's a good time to catch him/her? And is there a better number for them?\"</li>\n<li><b>\"What's it about?\":</b> \"I'd like to show them a free redesign of their homepage. Takes 15 minutes.\"</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>10. Voicemail (under 20 seconds)</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi <b>[name]</b>, this is Johnny, a local web designer. I came across <b>[business]</b> on Google, y'all have great reviews. I'd love to build y'all a free refresh of your website and show it to you side by side. Call or text me at <b>832-508-0059</b>. Again, 832-508-0059.\"</blockquote>\n<h3>11. Text after a voicemail or no answer</h3>\n<blockquote class=\"say\">\"Hi [name], it's Johnny, local web designer. Just left you a voicemail. I'd love to build [business] a free refresh of your website and show it to you side by side on a quick 15-min Zoom. No cost unless you love it. 832-508-0059\"</blockquote>\n<h3>12. The meeting (15 minutes)</h3>\n<p>1. Quick thanks, ask how business is going (1 min).</p>\n<p>2. Show both sites side by side on their phone or the Zoom screen. Point out what's better: easy to read on a phone, tap-to-call, their newer photos, reviews up front (3-5 min).</p>\n<p>3. Ask: \"What do you think? Anything you'd change?\" Write it all down.</p>\n<p>4. <b>Likes it:</b> \"Awesome. It's 200 to switch and it's yours. Do you want me to host and manage it, or handle that yourself?\" Send the payment link from the CRM. CRM: <b>Won</b>.</p>\n<p>5. <b>Wants changes:</b> \"Easy, I'll fix those and send it over by [day].\" Ask Dex to revise.</p>\n<p>6. <b>No:</b> \"No worries at all. Do you know anyone else who could use one?\" Log the reason.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><b>Rules:</b> dial by hand, be honest, never promise anything not in Offer &amp; Pricing. Respect \"don't call me\" right away. Log every call in the CRM.</p>"};
